meta {
  name: Login
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: https://localhost:51629/Account/Login
  body: formUrlEncoded
  auth: none
}

body:form-urlencoded {
  Email: admin@example.edu
  Password: {{adminPassword}}
  __RequestVerificationToken: {{antiforgeryToken}}
}

docs {
  Sign in with the email and password of an active account provisioned by
  database/seed-local-admin.sql. There is no default account.

  The login form is antiforgery-protected, so a bare POST returns 400:
  1. GET /Account/Login in the browser (or in Bruno) and copy the
     __RequestVerificationToken hidden input value.
  2. Set the collection variables adminPassword and antiforgeryToken.
  3. Send this request. A successful sign-in returns 302 to /Home/Index and
     sets the non-persistent AttendTa.Auth cookie, which Bruno reuses for the
     other requests in this collection.

  A wrong password, an unknown email and an inactive account all return 200
  with the same "Incorrect email or password." message and no cookie.

  Logout is POST /Account/Logout with the same antiforgery token; GET returns 405.
}
